{title: What shall we do with the drunken sailor}
{artist: Traditional Sea Shanty}
{key: Em}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 120}

{comment: Strophe 1}
[Em]What shall we do with the drunken sailor?
[D]What shall we do with the drunken sailor?
[Em]What shall we do with the drunken sailor?
[Em]Ear-[D]ly in the [Em]morning

{comment: Refrain}
[Em]Hooray, and up she rises
[D]Hooray, and up she rises
[Em]Hooray, and up she rises
[Em]Ear-[D]ly in the [Em]morning

{comment: Strophe 2}
[Em]Put him in the long boat 'til he's sober
